{"availability":"available","full":"edison16a/SandboxLabML","name":"SandboxLabML","description":"Interactive model creation through machine learning in the browser","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-06T09:31:31Z","updated":"2026-10-18T09:47:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sandboxlabs.vercel.app/","topics":[],"demo":"https://sandboxlabs.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T19:16:12.241Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T19:16:12.241Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T19:16:12.241Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:23.800Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T22:36:52.397Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-12T11:45:42.749Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T19:16:12.241Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A live machine learning lab in your browser, where you watch neural networks learn to race and play hide and seek in 3D."],"features":["Real neuroevolution. Brains evolve with NEAT, which starts from tiny networks and grows them. Mutations add links and neurons, and speciation protects new ideas long enough to improve.","Real physics. Racing uses a tire model with a grip limit. Hide and Seek runs on the Rapier physics engine, so crates are pushed and blocked by real contacts.","Fully reproducible. Every random number is seeded and every weight is stored exactly. Replays are re-simulated from stored brains instead of recorded video, and a test checks a replay matches its training run tick for…","Benchmarked. A built-in benchmark scores any model on held-out tracks or against fixed reference champions, so you can tell real learning from overfitting.","Private by default. Everything runs locally in Web Workers. Runs are saved in your browser and can be exported as a file to share."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/edison16a/SandboxLabML/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e9197a44a4d1b680ddfb